sentences.l:
And of them, as flakes of snow fall thick
on a wintry day, when counsellor Zeus has roused himself
to snow on men, making known his own shafts;

So of them to both sides the stones flew thick,
some then at the Trojans, others from the Trojans at the Achaeans,
the men being pelted;

not untried is he minded to be driven from the steading,
but he, then, either snatches, leaping upon one, or he himself too
is struck among the foremost, from a swift hand, by a javelin;

and he noticed the two Ajaxes, insatiate of war,
standing, and Teucer, newly from the hut
coming, near at hand;

for so great a thud there was, and the cry reached heaven,
of shields being struck and horse-plumed helms
and gates;
